<<<
ne’er-do-weel, ne’er-do-well,. The Scotch spelling is recommended. The OED’s remark is: ‘ The word being of northern & Sc. origin, the form -weel is freq. employed even by southern writers °.
===
**ne'er-do-weel, ne'er-do-well.** The Scotch spelling is recommended. The OED's remark is: 'The word being of northern & Sc. origin, the form *-weel* is freq. employed even by southern writers'.
>>>

