negative. ‘The answer is in the negative’ is Parliament language, but deserves much severer condemnation (as a pompous PERI- PHRASIS for No, sir) than most of the expressions described as unparliamentary language.
===
**negative.** 'The answer is in the negative' is Parliament language, but deserves much severer condemnation (as a pompous ^^PERIPHRASIS^^ for No, sir) than most of the expressions described as unparliamentary language.
>>>

